# Temperance marker — brass chip + condensed figlet
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: feat/brass-mark
- scope-decision: Right thing — replace a mark that is provably broken
  (Monaco carries neither half-block; 73% fill blobs on line spacing) with
  one that cannot fail. Right way — pure-ASCII figlet at install, brass chip
  everywhere else, both verified against the four common terminal fonts.
- blast-radius: src/lib/init-brand-mark.ts and its one caller at
  src/commands/init.ts:769. The existing tests pin the OLD contract (11 rows,
  27 cols, four codepoints, min 53) and will fail by design — this is a
  deliberate redesign, not a regression.
- verification: figlet is 4 rows x 40 cols, every row even width, and every
  character is printable ASCII. Assert that mechanically, not by eye.
- drift-trigger: If this branch starts collapsing the 206-line file inventory,
  stop. That is a separate concern and its own PR. Also stop if the bass clef
  glyph reappears — deferred to cli#475 by operator decision.
